            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sugarplum"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious and super healthy too! We really loved the flavor combinations. I followed the directions exactly for the first omelet and then I made another omelet and the second time I folded the veggie mixture into the middle. It stayed together better. This was the perfect ,healthy low-carb, yummy way to start the day off right!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kangrrl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added sliced new potatoes and kohlrabi greens instead of spinach, turned out really delicious! Even my pickiest kid enjoyed it. A trick I learned long ago was to use a large cast iron skillet. After eggs are added, turn heat to low until about halfway cooked through. Put skillet under broiler for ~4-5 mins to cook the top. This prevents total destruction while attempting to flip omelet, and it ends up looking picture perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-27T16:33:34.500Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SPROUT117"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As a really great cook, I already make a great omelette....and then I made this recipe. amazing! I was surprised that the addition of nutmeg was so good along with the addition of cheese INTO the eggs rather than on the veggies. I adjusted the omelette for one using two egg whites and one egg-it still came out thick. The only change that I would make is to cook the veggies and then add them into the omelette because the spinach can burn if the egg doesn't get under it properly. This will be my new \"normal\" omelette. Also very heavy so you don't hungry all day. Last note: added zaatar and feta to the top of it...and dill in with the tomatoes - not needed but delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-11T11:31:23.520Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jim hall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "fro me, too fussy with separating the eggs - teo eggs for a single serving, cook in butter, keep moving the eggs to get an even cook and when the eggs are just shy of solid, fold them over - delicious with cheese or mushrooms or ham or onions or.....",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-19T18:26:47.507Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shimmy Justabit"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Five stars....!!! For WHOLE. EGG. Omelets. We must stop propagating this terrible myth that egg whites, without yolk, or less yolk, are somehow healthier. Eggs are a symbiotic creation! And that myth was disproven a long time ago. Annnnd omelettes taste *far* better with whole eggs...\n\nChange that, and you've got a five-star winner!\n\nI also recommend the folding of at least half of the veggies inside.. they keep more of their original shape/texture/mouth-feel that way, and it holds the omelet together nicely.",
            "datePublished": "2017-12-01T18:57:28.633Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "voraciousgirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Changed up the method a bit. Cooked the mushroom/pepper/green onion mixture first. Removed from pan &amp; added egg. Then added veggies along with spinach to the egg. Light &amp; easy breakfast.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-07T09:36:18.017Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Fox"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The combo of spices and veggies suggested are perfect! I did use another reviewer's suggestion and changed the directions slightly. I sauteed the veggies and then added them AFTER the egg mixture had set (cooked). I was able to use one pan for everything by sauteeing veggies first, then transferring them to a saucer while the egg mixture was cooking. Once that's done, put the veggies on one side of the omelet and fold over.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-15T15:38:21.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good! no trouble with it at all..I did use two whole jumbo eggs, half the spinach as i had less egg...\nthen cut the omelette in half when cooked.....will definitely be a keeper recipe. Thanks for posting!",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-26T15:55:06.157Z"
          },
          {
